<section id="format-vs-package">
  <h2>Format version <code>v0.4</code> vs package release <code>0.4.0</code></h2>

  <p>
    <strong><code>v0.4</code> is the schema format version</strong> — the set of
    contracts under <code>/schemas/v0.4/</code> and the v0.4 section of these
    docs. <strong><code>0.4.0</code> is the npm release version</strong> of
    <code>@designlasagna/schemas</code> that ships those files
    (<code>@designlasagna/schemas@0.4.0</code>, import paths
    <code>@designlasagna/schemas/v0.4/*.json</code>). The two move together but
    are different things:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      In a manifest's <code>$schema</code>, use the format version in the URL:
      <code>https://designlasagna.recipes/schemas/v0.4/tokens.json</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      In a native manifest's <code>schemaVersion</code> field (a plain semver
      string), write <code>"0.4.0"</code> for a v0.4-format manifest —
      <code>"0.3.0"</code> for one that stays on v0.3.
    </li>
    <li>
      When installing or importing contracts, pin the package release:
      <code>@designlasagna/schemas@0.4.0</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    See the <a href="/docs/schemas/">schema overview</a> for the same
    format-vs-release distinction.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="lifecycle-selection">
  <h2>Lifecycle selection</h2>

  <dl class="schema-list">
    <div>
      <dt class="schema-list__title">Native manifests</dt>
      <dd><span class="schema-list__label">Opt in</span> Per document: v0.4 <code>$schema</code> URL and <code>schemaVersion: "0.4.0"</code></dd>
      <dd><span class="schema-list__label">Otherwise</span> The document stays on v0.3</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="schema-list__title">CEM</dt>
      <dd><span class="schema-list__label">Opt in</span> Select lifecycle profile <code>0.4</code> in project or resolver config</dd>
      <dd><span class="schema-list__label">Otherwise</span> Legacy profile; v0.4 fields are not applied</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="schema-list__title">DTCG</dt>
      <dd><span class="schema-list__label">Opt in</span> Select lifecycle profile <code>0.4</code> in project or resolver config</dd>
      <dd><span class="schema-list__label">Otherwise</span> Legacy profile; v0.4 fields are not applied</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <p>
    Nothing converts automatically; the full selection rules are in the
    <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.4/lifecycle/#lifecycle-selection">lifecycle reference</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="per-contract">
  <h2>What changed per contract</h2>

  <p>
    The per-contract breakdown, with breaking changes marked, is in the
    <a href="/tools/schemas/changelog/#v0-4-0">v0.4.0 changelog entry</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="unchanged">
  <h2>What did not change</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Root manifest requirements; <code>schemaVersion</code> is still a plain string.</li>
    <li>Extension namespaces: the CEM <code>$extensions</code> key and DTCG <code>recipes.designlasagna</code>.</li>
    <li>Deprecation records still require <code>message</code>; <code>removal</code> and <code>replacement</code> stay optional strings.</li>
    <li>v0.3 documents stay valid against the hosted v0.3 contracts.</li>
    <li>v0.2 contracts are untouched.</li>
  </ul>
</section>


